ontology_mapping:
  ontology_id: kgmicrobe.ingredient:ferrous_ammonium_sulfate_heptahydrate_nominal_0_1_percent_wv_stock
  ontology_label: Nominal 0.1% w/v ferrous ammonium sulfate heptahydrate stock
  ontology_source: kgmicrobe.ingredient
  mapping_quality: FALLBACK_REGISTRY
  evidence:
  - evidence_type: CURATOR_JUDGMENT
    source: https://togomedium.org/medium/M2625
    notes: DSMZ718 specifies 2 ml of a 0.1% w/v preparation named Fe(NH4)2(SO4)2 x
      7 H2O. The source heptahydrate claim is preserved and is not replaced by the
      familiar hexahydrate. Solvent is unstated; the whole stock has its own identity.
      No verified exact eligible ontology term or existing whole-preparation owner
      was established by the bounded source/owner review. This self-registry mapping
      represents the preparation, not its individual constituents.
  - evidence_type: LLM_SUGGESTION
    source: https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium399.pdf
    notes: 'Source-qualified 0.1% w/v stock as explicitly supplied in https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium399.pdf.
      0.1 g per 100 mL is represented as 1 g/L. The receiving addition volume is not
      stock concentration. The source does not disclose stock solvent or other constituents;
      these are not inferred, and component completeness is UNKNOWN. This whole stock
      is not identical to its solute. The bare ingredient label is retained in these
      notes and frozen case evidence, not as a stock synonym. Raw source label: ''Fe(NH4)2(SO4)2
      x 7 H2O''; source ID: mediadive.ingredient:456.'
  - evidence_type: LLM_SUGGESTION
    source: https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium718.pdf; https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium399.pdf
    notes: 'Shared nominal preparation scope supported by DSMZ718 andDSMZ399: both
      explicitly name Fe(NH4)2(SO4)2 x7H2O at0.1%w/v and a2mLreceiving addition. 0.1g/100mL
      equals1g/L. These facts justify one represented known material scope rather
      than two candidates distinguished only by recipe number. Neither source supplies
      solvent/full formulation, so this is not complete-composition equivalence; UNKNOWN
      closure and all exact-source/owner holds remain. Literal seven waters are retained,
      without substitution of conventional Mohr hexahydrate. No receiving gas atmosphere
      is a stock constituent.'
